# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed by /bin/sh inside Linux images.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) a checkout rewrites
# LF to CRLF, and the trailing \r becomes part of the token: `set -eu` turns
# into `set -eu\r` and BusyBox sh aborts with "set: illegal option -".
# docker/staff-ui/rehash-patched-assets.sh failed exactly this way, so the
# staff-ui image could not build at all on a Windows clone.
#
# Forcing LF for these files makes the working tree match what the container
# runs, regardless of anyone's local autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*/Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/**/Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# SQL is piped into psql inside Linux pods.
ci/commons-services/**/*.sql text eol=lf
